msgid "A working end-to-end search against the top 500 sites:"
msgstr "Une recherche complète et fonctionnelle sur les 500 premiers sites :"

#: ../../source/library-usage.rst:52 1b8d59523b644de2826a34890bb83005
msgid "Key points:"
msgstr "Points importants :"

#: ../../source/library-usage.rst:54 9febe61ea25341fe89f67792bce0dd7b
msgid ""
"``maigret_search`` is an ``async`` function — wrap it with "
"``asyncio.run(...)`` or ``await`` it from inside your own event loop."
msgstr ""
"``maigret_search`` est une fonction ``async`` : encapsulez-la dans "
"``asyncio.run(...)`` ou faites ``await`` depuis votre propre boucle "
"d'événements."

#: ../../source/library-usage.rst:55 94cba639a3fd48d59f757a97923bbcce
msgid ""
"``is_parsing_enabled=True`` turns on ``socid_extractor`` so "
"``result[\"ids_data\"]`` is populated with profile fields (bio, linked "
"accounts, uids, etc.). See its `Library usage <https://socid-"
"extractor.readthedocs.io/en/latest/library-usage.html>`_ page for calling"
" it directly, and `Maigret integration <https://socid-"
"extractor.readthedocs.io/en/latest/maigret-integration.html>`_ for how "
"the two projects fit together."
msgstr ""
"``is_parsing_enabled=True`` active ``socid_extractor``, si bien que "
"``result[\"ids_data\"]`` est rempli avec les champs du profil "
"(biographie, comptes liés, uids, etc.). Voir sa page `Library usage "
"<https://socid-extractor.readthedocs.io/en/latest/library-usage.html>`_ "
"pour l'appeler directement, et `Maigret integration <https://socid-"
"extractor.readthedocs.io/en/latest/maigret-integration.html>`_ pour "
"comprendre comment les deux projets s'articulent."

#: ../../source/library-usage.rst:56 9d8f67adc20e46818a07c55a1e8d0d1c
msgid ""
"Each entry in the returned dict has a ``\"status\"`` object with "
"``is_found()``, plus ``url_user``, ``http_status``, ``rank``, "
"``ids_data``, and more."
msgstr ""
"Chaque entrée du dictionnaire renvoyé contient un objet ``\"status\"`` "
"avec ``is_found()``, ainsi que ``url_user``, ``http_status``, ``rank``, "
"``ids_data``, et d'autres champs."

